{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The read path has a distinct authority question: its singleton fast path checks that one voter remains, but not that the responder is that voter. With `StepDownOnRemoval=false`, a removed leader can remain in leader state. I’ll explore whether it can issue a ReadState after the remaining voter commits later work, while keeping caller applicability and the documented application-wait rule unresolved.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > explore_removed_read_test.go <<'GO'\npackage raft\nimport (\n \\\"testing\\\"\n \\\"fmt\\\"\n \\\"encoding/json\\\"\n pb \\\"go.etcd.io/raft/v3/raftpb\\\"\n)\nfunc TestAssuranceExploreRemovedRead(t *testing.T){\n for _,stepDown:=range []bool{false,true}{\n  t.Run(fmt.Sprintf(\\\"stepdown_%v\\\",stepDown),func(t *testing.T){\n   must:=func(err error){if err\"'!=nil{t.Fatal(err)}}\n   emit:=func(event string,f map[string]interface{}){f[\"event\"]=event;f[\"step_down\"]=stepDown;b,err:=json.Marshal(f);must(err);fmt.Println(\"CA_EVENT \"+string(b))}\n   nodes:=map[uint64]*RawNode{};stores:=map[uint64]*MemoryStorage{};applied:=map[uint64]uint64{};values:=map[uint64]string{}\n   isolated:=false\n   for id:=uint64(1);id<=2;id++ {st:=NewMemoryStorage();stores[id]=st;n,err:=NewRawNode(&Config{ID:id,ElectionTick:10,HeartbeatTick:1,Storage:st,MaxSizePerMsg:4096,MaxInflightMsgs:16,ReadOnlyOption:ReadOnlySafe,StepDownOnRemoval:stepDown});must(err);nodes[id]=n;must(n.Bootstrap([]Peer{{ID:1},{ID:2}}))}\n   pump:=func(){\n    for round:=0;round<1000;round++{\n     did:=false;var msgs []pb.Message\n     for id:=uint64(1);id<=2;id++{n:=nodes[id];if !n.HasReady(){continue};did=true;rd:=n.Ready();if !IsEmptySnap(rd.Snapshot){t.Fatal(\"unexpected snapshot\")};must(stores[id].Append(rd.Entries));if !IsEmptyHardState(rd.HardState){must(stores[id].SetHardState(rd.HardState))}\n      for _,m:=range rd.Messages{b,err:=m.Marshal();must(err);var cp pb.Message;must(cp.Unmarshal(b));msgs=append(msgs,cp)}\n      for _,ent:=range rd.CommittedEntries{switch ent.Type{case pb.EntryConfChange:var cc pb.ConfChange;must(cc.Unmarshal(ent.Data));n.ApplyConfChange(cc);case pb.EntryNormal:if len(ent.Data)>0{values[id]=string(ent.Data)}};applied[id]=ent.Index}\n      for _,rs:=range rd.ReadStates{emit(\"read_state\",map[string]interface{}{\"node\":id,\"index\":rs.Index,\"context\":string(rs.RequestCtx),\"app_applied\":applied[id],\"app_value\":values[id],\"role\":n.BasicStatus().RaftState.String(),\"term\":n.BasicStatus().Term,\"voters\":n.Status().Config.Voters[0].Slice()})}\n      n.Advance(rd)\n     }\n     for _,m:=range msgs{if isolated&&m.From!=m.To {emit(\"partition_drop\",map[string]interface{}{\"from\":m.From,\"to\":m.To,\"type\":m.Type.String()});continue};err:=nodes[m.To].Step(m);if err!=ErrStepPeerNotFound{must(err)}}\n     if !did{return}\n    };t.Fatal(\"driver failed to drain\")\n   }\n   pump();must(nodes[1].Campaign());pump();must(nodes[1].Propose([]byte(\"old\")));pump()\n   must(nodes[1].ProposeConfChange(pb.ConfChange{Type:pb.ConfChangeRemoveNode,NodeID:1}));pump()\n   emit(\"removed\",map[string]interface{}{\"node1_role\":nodes[1].BasicStatus().RaftState.String(),\"node1_voters\":nodes[1].Status().Config.Voters[0].Slice(),\"node2_voters\":nodes[2].Status().Config.Voters[0].Slice(),\"applied1\":applied[1],\"applied2\":applied[2]})\n   isolated=true;must(nodes[2].Campaign());pump();must(nodes[2].Propose([]byte(\"new\")));pump()\n   emit(\"write_applied\",map[string]interface{}{\"node\":2,\"applied\":applied[2],\"value\":values[2],\"role\":nodes[2].BasicStatus().RaftState.String(),\"term\":nodes[2].BasicStatus().Term})\n   nodes[1].ReadIndex([]byte(\"read-after-new-write\"));pump()\n   emit(\"drained\",map[string]interface{}{\"ready1\":nodes[1].HasReady(),\"ready2\":nodes[2].HasReady(),\"applied1\":applied[1],\"value1\":values[1]})\n  })\n }\n}\nGO\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,subprocess\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'))\ns={'action':'explore','question':'With ReadOnlySafe and StepDownOnRemoval=false, can a removed leader whose installed config is singleton {2} issue a local ReadState after node 2 independently becomes leader and applies a later write? Compare StepDownOnRemoval=true. This explores response eligibility, not yet an endpoint safety verdict; caller removal duties and the strict application-index wording remain contract questions.','rationale':'A sourced discrepancy connects membership loss to the singleton ReadIndex fast path: switchToConfig may retain leader role after self-removal, and IsSingleton checks cardinality without self-membership. Use actual bootstrap, election, committed self-removal, partition and later write to test reachability; do not fabricate term or membership.','harness_path':'explore_removed_read_test.go','sources':[dict(id='s-read-safe-contract',file='raft.go',start_line=56,end_line=67,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='s-removal-option',file='raft.go',start_line=280,end_line=285,kind='interface_statement'),dict(id='s-singleton',file='tracker/tracker.go',start_line=158,end_line=163,kind='code_observation'),dict(id='s-read-caller-contract',file='node.go',start_line=219,end_line=229,kind='interface_statement')],'feedback':{'ref_ids':['B-read','B-config','s-read-caller-contract','s-singleton','src-config','s-leader'],'answered':'ReadIndex explicitly allows request loss and assigns retry to the caller, so missing release of a request alone is not an automatic-continuation obligation. A separate authority premise is unresolved: the singleton fast path is based on voter cardinality, while default self-removal can preserve leader state.','remaining':['Execute the legal self-removal and later-write history.','Determine whether caller contracts require stopping a removed node before ReadIndex, and distinguish a returned index from completion under the documented application wait rule.'],'understanding':'updated','rationale':'The selected exploration prioritizes a possible authority/safety discrepancy over another request-loss liveness hypothesis; applicability is not assumed.'}}\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2);print(subprocess.run(r['validation']['command']+['submission.json'],capture_output=True,text=True).stdout)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
